    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our undisputed catalyst; his 79.76 score is anchored by a favorable matchup against Sasaki and a massive boost from his elite speed profile. With the ability to exploit Sasaki\u2019s pace, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine for stolen bases, a category we are prioritizing aggressively. Alongside him, **Brice Turang** (70.39) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.44) provide significant upside. **Brice Turang** benefits from a premium leadoff spot and a high-probability SB environment against Matthews, while **Mickey Moniak** secures a massive +14% platoon edge against Leahy, making him a high-efficiency play despite the park factor drag.\n\nOur most difficult decision occurred at the fringe of the starting rotation, where **Cole Young** (33.73) fell just short of a lineup berth. While **Cole Young** offers a solid baseline, he was ultimately downgraded by a brutal matchup against Rasmussen, whose 3.19 xERA provides minimal opportunity for the offensive production required to justify the cap hit. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley** (49.53). While his projected score holds him in the lineup, the 38% rain risk is a notable concern. If the weather reports deteriorate, we may be forced to pull **Austin Riley** to preserve our game caps.\n\nFinally, we are closely monitoring the lineup confirmation for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes**. Both have strong projections based on their assumed spots in the order\u2014**Gabriel Moreno** at #3 and **Isaac Paredes** against the soft xERA of Ray\u2014but their actualized value is highly dependent on those batting positions holding firm. We remain without the services of **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** due to injury, but with the high-upside speed profiles of our active core, we are well-positioned to gain ground in the 5x5 standings today.",
